  "lineage": "Late-1990s-and-2000s producer-team-era contemporary R&B aesthetic codified by the Darkchild, Jam-and-Lewis (later Flyte Tyme), Timbaland, She'kspere, and Rodney Jerkins production-lineage. Built on the breath-admixed close-miked intimate-vocal-aesthetic with stacked harmony backgrounds (typically 4-to-8 voice layered), neo-soul jazz-extended chord-vocabulary (minor-9, major-7-sharp-11, sus-2, sus-4 voicings), and programmed drum-machine kit (typically Roland TR-909, Akai MPC60-3000, or Korg M1) playing swung-and-shuffled hi-hat-and-snare-with-808-kick. The genre layered Atlanta-Memphis-NYC studio-clusters and bridged classic-Motown-and-Philly-soul lineage to 2010s-modern-R&B and trap-soul.",
